NUM-14: no evaporation from a storage unit holding less than FUDGE

storage_getLosses() multiplies the evaporation rate (ft/s) by the surface
area only when the unit holds more than FUDGE (1e-4 ft3). Otherwise it
left the bare ft/s rate in evapRate and returned it as a loss in cfs, so a
nearly empty unit lost rate x dt ft3 per step whatever its area, and booked
it as evaporation. Set the rate to 0 in that case, as SWMM 5.1.013 did
before 5.1.014 moved the FUDGE test from the whole loss block to the
evaporation term only. Seepage is unchanged.
The 6.0.0 router had zeroed this case and was changed to copy legacy;
the comment describing that is replaced.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-14_swmm600.patch

